{"_meta":{"openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Chart cast","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Casting the chart"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Use this when someone wants their Tu Vi (Zi Wei Dou Shu, \u7d2b\u5fae\u6597\u6570) birth chart or its reading. Pass `birth_date` (solar, YYYY-MM-DD, 1921 to 2100), `birth_time` (local HH:MM, 24-hour) and `gender`. Optional: `calendar` (vi, the default, or zh), `leap_month` (split, same or next), `late_zi` (next_day or same_day for a 23:00 birth), `topics`. Returns the lunar date, the 12 palaces with the 14 main stars, 14 minor stars, the four transformations and the 10-year periods, in Vietnamese and Chinese, plus readings for births from 1950 to 2026 from an open CC BY dataset, each with citations to the classic \u7d2b\u5fae\u6597\u6570\u5168\u4e66. Keep the `attribution` with any reading you repeat. Readings are cultural, not predictions.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"A birth date, clock time and gender, plus optional calendar rules.","examples":[{"birth_date":"1990-03-12","birth_time":"14:30","gender":"male","topics":["career"]}],"properties":{"birth_date":{"description":"Birth date on the solar (Gregorian) calendar, YYYY-MM-DD, from 1921 to 2100","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"birth_time":{"description":"Local clock time of birth, HH:MM in 24-hour form. 23:00 to 00:59 is the T\u00fd hour","pattern":"^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$","type":"string"},"calendar":{"default":"vi","description":"Lunar calendar and tradition: vi is the Vietnamese calendar (UTC+7 from 1968, UTC+8 before) with M\u1ec7nh ch\u1ee7 by year branch; zh the Chinese one (UTC+8) with \u547d\u4e3b by Life-palace branch","enum":["vi","zh"],"type":"string"},"gender":{"description":"Gender at birth; it sets the direction of the 10-year periods","enum":["male","female"],"type":"string"},"late_zi":{"default":"next_day","descriptio